# CivitMatrix UI — Win95, browser, lightweight

## Stack

- **Browser-only UI** served locally (no Electron/Tauri unless explicitly requested).
- Keep it **lightweight**: prefer vanilla HTML/CSS/JS or a tiny dependency set. Avoid heavy SPA stacks by default.
- Reuse the existing Python CLI/engine; the UI orchestrates it — don’t fork download logic into JS.

## Visual language (default theme: Win95)

- Classic Windows 95 look: silver-gray chrome (`#c0c0c0`), navy active title bars, teal desktop (`#008080`), 3D beveled borders (light top/left, dark bottom/right).
- UI controls: raised/sunken panels, chunky buttons, inset text fields, menu bar, status bar, system font stack (`"MS Sans Serif", "Segoe UI", Tahoma, sans-serif`).
- Green “Installed” / success accents may nod to SM, but don’t break the Win95 palette with neon/purple gradients.
- **Later:** add a theme switcher (Win95 default + modern). Build with CSS variables so skins can swap without rewriting markup.

## Workflow

- Local planning stays in gitignored `todo.md` — never commit it.
- Ship only after the feature is **tested and working**: commit public files → push `ArturoWolff/civitmatrix`.
- Never commit `.env`, API keys, logs, downloads, or personal absolute paths.

